Package: visualR
Type: Package
Title: Palindrome-Addressed Topological Runtime
Version: 0.5.0
Date: 2026-08-09
Authors@R:
    person("lkh-cq", given = NULL, email = "lkh-cq@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: lkh-cq [aut, cre]
Maintainer: lkh-cq <lkh-cq@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: A palindrome-addressed topological runtime with three-layer
    architecture: palindrome storage, matrix computation emergence,
    and projection view. Pure-R semantic correctness for PAL state
    construction, format/parse serialization, palindrome unfold/fold,
    jiugong grid mapping, diamond order field, frozen symmetry
    operations, and validation. v0.1.1 hardens serialization against
    arbitrary code execution. v0.2 adds palindrome grammar interop,
    closure gate, emergence operators, Gamma generator, peel chain,
    S_5 carrier, and R interactive+concurrent layer
    (pal_pipe / batch_compute / interact). v0.2.1 Semantic Hardening:
    mapping-pack dependency injection (fail-closed), unified carrier
    dispatch, closed token domain, closure fact / transition policy
    separation. v0.2.2 P0 completion: full-content pack hash with
    assert_pack on resolve (fail closed on tamper), pack drives ALL
    mappings (gamma_rule / local_center_transform / carrier_fn), typed
    carrier dispatch (non-3x3 carriers are views, not compute paths),
    operator ABI enforced at registration and call time, strict
    S_4-only pal_to_jiugong + general pal_to_square_view, hard offset
    validation in diamond_at, GitHub Actions CI (Linux/Windows/macOS,
    release/oldrel/devel). v0.3.0 B-Promotion: 3 experimental markers
    (carrier_11x11 / Gamma lowercasing / closure recurse) promoted to
    FROZEN with added coverage, metadata/lifecycle aligned. R
    interactive-concurrent is the benchmark; Python mapping_pack.py is
    glue/cross-validation only.
